---
// Leaderboard (#/leaderboard): the best of each class on the climb to chaining two facts
// (thorp.leaderboard.payload, /api/leaderboard). Climb: per chain, the rungs performed from the bottom
// plus the next rung's share of its mark, averaged over the four chains (0 to 5). Chaining lift: the
// mean lift on the four 50m rungs, the north star. UI.md, "Leaderboard".
---
<div class="section" id="leaderboard">
  <h1>Leaderboard <span class="q">the best in class on the climb to chaining two facts. Every class must climb closer to chaining two facts than the class beneath; the 50m attempts it</span></h1>
  <section class="panel" id="smokingqwen">
    <h2>Smoking Qwen <span class="note">P(a 400M Thorp chains two facts as well as Qwen3 4B): Thorp's classes, chaining lift against size, fitted and carried an order of magnitude below Qwen3 4B; the Mac cannot train 400M, so the proof is a forecast (thorp/smoking_qwen.py; DECISIONS.md, "Smoking Qwen, pre-registered")</span></h2>
    <div class="sqhead" id="sqhead"></div>
    <div class="row sqrow">
      <div class="chart tall" id="sqchart"></div>
      <div class="sqside">
        <div class="k">Does the method work? <span class="s">the same fit where the answer is known</span></div>
        <div id="sqbacktest"></div>
        <div class="k mt">The rule <span class="s">pre-registered</span></div>
        <p class="s" id="sqrule"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Best in class <span class="note">each class's best run by its climb (0 to 5: on each of the four chains, the rungs performed from the bottom without a gap, plus the next rung's lift as a share of its mark; the mean of the four), ticked at each rung; beside it the chaining lift, the mean lift on the four 50m rungs (two facts chained), performed at <b id="lbthr"></b>; stalled when a class climbs no higher than the class beneath</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="lbboard" data-nosort><thead><tr><th>class</th><th>best run</th><th>climb</th><th>chaining lift</th><th>the four chains</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel">
    <h2>The reference ladder <span class="note">outside models read on the same pairs, on the same bars, for scale; the largest is the perch</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="lbref" data-nosort><thead><tr><th>model</th><th>climb</th><th>chaining lift</th><th>the four chains</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Every run <span class="note">every run with chain readings (its latest), by climb</span></h2>
    <div class="handtools"><span class="note">class</span><select id="lbclass"><option value="">every class</option></select><span class="note" id="lbcount"></span></div>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="lbruns"><thead><tr><th>run</th><th>ship</th><th>class</th><th>status</th><th>climb</th><th>chaining lift</th><th>the four chains</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
</div>
